{{also|Tauchen}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{term|tuchen|lang=gmh}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|-tūhhan|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|dūkaną|lang=gem-pro}}. Compare {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|duiken|lang=nl}}, English [[duck]] (verb).

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|tau|chen}}
* {{IPA|/ˈtaʊ̯χən/|[ˈtʰaʊ̯χn̩]|lang=de}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb-weak|taucht|tauchte|getaucht|auxiliary=both}}

# to [[dive]]
# {{figuratively|lang=de}} to [[bathe]]
#* '''2010''', ''[[w:Der Spiegel|Der Spiegel]]'', issue [http://www.spiegel.de/spiegel/print/index-2010-22.html 22/2010], page 133:
#*:Die Sonne steht inzwischen tief und '''taucht''' die Landschaft in ein sanftes Licht.
#*::By now the sun is low and bathes the landscape in a gentle light.

